# T-1481: field_annotations implementation — @Child field annotation produces role in annotation dict.
# Named-field constructor with @Child on a compound type expression (no explicit role: key in
# annotation) produces the default role "One". The role is never inferred from the type name —
# only an explicit role: key in the annotation determines the role.
#
# The "Seq" role no longer exists — @Child on [Seq T] produces "One", not "Seq".
# Use @Child@[role: "MapValues"] to declare MapValues; no other non-default role is recognized.
[NodeType: [type Union@[as-type: [fn [let u] u]  guarding: False]: [
  items@Child: [Seq NodeType]]]]
[ann: [annotation-of NodeType.Union]]
[has-field-anns: [has? "field-annotations" ann]]
[role: [get "role" [get "items" [get "field-annotations" ann]]]]
[result: [and has-field-anns [= role "One"]]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Variant(Boolean.True, Null)})
